# Porto Features - Cursor Rules

## Project Purpose

Shared BDD contracts (Gherkin) and fixtures aligned with [porto-data](https://github.com/gruncellka/porto-data). Step definitions and execution live outside this repo.

## Structure

```
porto_features/                     # Published package content
├── errors.json                     # PORTO_* catalog
├── features/
│   ├── sdk/
│   │   ├── core/                   # @sdk @core
│   │   └── providers/{operator}/   # @sdk @operator:{id}
│   └── adapters/{operator}/{integration}/
│       ├── marks.feature           # @adapters @canary / @heavy
│       └── errors.feature          # @error + unique @scenario:
└── fixtures/                       # Test data
    └── addresses/
```

Coverage indexes (`sdk.yaml`, `orders.generated.yaml`, …) live in Porto SDK Lab `labs/matrix/` — not in this package.

## Gherkin Format

Every Feature declares exactly one of `@sdk` or `@adapters`. Paid purchase uses `When I create a mark`. Do not add fake simulate / stamp-generation features — offline resolve is `When I resolve the letter`. See `docs/vocabulary.md` and `docs/scenario-policy.md`.

## Key Principles

- **Implementation-agnostic**: Features describe behavior, not runner internals
- **Data-driven**: Use fixtures for test data
- **BDD**: Business-readable scenarios
- **Package-first**: Keep data under `porto_features/` so npm and PyPI ship identical files

## Generated adapter matrix

`labs/matrix/orders.generated.yaml` and adapter `mark_order` Examples are produced from porto-data wire by Porto SDK Lab `matrix-orders-sync.py` — do not hand-edit.

## Do NOT

- Add step definitions here — those belong in implementor test suites
- Reference runner internals in feature files
- Duplicate fixtures that exist in porto-data
- Ship `contracts/` or `porto_features/matrix/` in this package
- Add `mark_simulate` / `stamp_generation` / CLI stamp-simulate scenarios
